	<body>
		<title>
			<p>Nested Sections</p>
		</title>
		<epigraph>
			<p>Every part has a chapter, and every chapter has a scene.</p>
			<text-author>The fixture</text-author>
		</epigraph>
		<section id="part1">
			<title>
				<p>Part One</p>
				<empty-line/>
				<p>The House</p>
			</title>
			<epigraph>
				<p>Nothing is simple when a door stands open.</p>
				<text-author>An old proverb</text-author>
			</epigraph>
			<section id="part1-ch1">
				<title>
					<p>Chapter 1. Arrival</p>
				</title>
				<section id="part1-ch1-s1">
					<title>
						<p>The Gate</p>
					</title>
					<p>The road ended at a wooden gate, and behind it a narrow path led up to the house.</p>
					<subtitle>At the door</subtitle>
					<p>Nobody answered the knock, so Anna pushed the door and stepped inside.</p>
					<empty-line/>
					<poem id="poem1">
						<title>
							<p>The Lantern</p>
						</title>
						<stanza>
							<v>A lantern in the hall,</v>
							<v>a shadow on the wall,</v>
						</stanza>
						<stanza>
							<v>a step upon the stair,</v>
							<v>and no one waiting there.</v>
						</stanza>
						<text-author>Anonymous</text-author>
					</poem>
				</section>
				<section id="part1-ch1-s2">
					<title>
						<p>The Letter</p>
					</title>
					<p>On the table lay a letter, folded twice and sealed with red wax.</p>
					<cite id="cite1">
						<p>Whoever reads this has come too late, or just in time.</p>
						<text-author>From the letter</text-author>
					</cite>
					<p>Anna read it twice and put it in her pocket.</p>
				</section>
			</section>
			<section id="part1-ch2">
				<title>
					<p>Chapter 2. The Inventory</p>
				</title>
				<section id="part1-ch2-s1">
					<title>
						<p>What the House Held</p>
					</title>
					<p>She counted everything she found in the three rooms.</p>
					<table id="table1">
						<tr>
							<th>Room</th>
							<th>Item</th>
							<th>Count</th>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Hall</td>
							<td>Lantern</td>
							<td>1</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Study</td>
							<td>Books</td>
							<td>212</td>
						</tr>
					</table>
					<p>The books, she decided, would take the longest.</p>
				</section>
			</section>
		</section>
	</body>
